      {
        "h_title": "Imperial",
        "main_title": "Goong pad sator - Bitter beans stir-fried with shrimp paste and prawns",
        "author": "John Chantarasak",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "2 tbsp of garlic, chopped",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/garlic-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/garlic-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "garlic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of gapi shrimp paste",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "5 tbsp of stink beans, peeled",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of vegetable oil",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "6 medium raw prawns",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/prawn-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/prawn-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "medium raw prawns"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "6 bird's eye chillies, chopped",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/chilli-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/chilli-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "bird's eye chillies"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of coriander root, chopped",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/coriander-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/coriander-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "coriander root"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tsp salt",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/salt-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/salt-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "salt"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "2 lime leaves, torn",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/lime-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/lime-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "lime leaves"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "2 tsp caster sugar",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of lime juice",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/lime-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/lime-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "lime juice"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "2 tsp fish sauce",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/fish-sauce-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/fish-sauce-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "fish sauce"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Method",
        "main_title": "Goong pad sator - Bitter beans stir-fried with shrimp paste and prawns",
        "author": "John Chantarasak",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Peel and remove the veins from the prawns, leaving the tails intact for presentation, if you wish. Place the prawn shells and heads in a tight fitting saucepan, cover with water and bring to a quick boil over a high heat, then reduce the heat and simmer for 5 minutes",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Skim any scum from the top of the prawn stock then pass through a sieve, pressing down the shells and heads with the back of a spoon to extract maximum flavour. Discard the shells and heads and set the stock aside",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "In a stone pestle and mortar, pound the chillies, garlic, coriander root and salt to a coarse paste. Add the shrimp paste and continue to work into the other ingredients. Set aside",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "3 tbsp of garlic, chopped",
            "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/garlic-recipes",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/collections/garlic-recipes",
                "anchor_text": "garlic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Bring a large saucepan of salted water to a rapid boil over a high heat. Add the stink/sator beans and blanche for 30 seconds before straining and refreshing with cold water. Drain well",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "5 tbsp of stink beans, peeled",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Heat the vegetable oil in a wok over a medium heat, then add the paste and stir-fry for 1 minute until fragrant. Add the peeled prawns, blanched stink/sator beans and torn lime leaves. Stir-fry together until the prawns are just cooked and have turned to an attractive pink colour, around 3 minutes",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "1 tbsp of vegetable oil",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Moisten with 5-6 tablespoons of the reserved prawn stock and season with the caster sugar, 1 teaspoon of the fish sauce and lime juice. Check for seasoning, and add more fish sauce if necessary - it should taste hot and umami salty. Transfer to a serving dish and eat with steamed rice",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "John is the co-founder of the restaurant AngloThai.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
